<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 29.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 29.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1 Tourism Asset	  3700.00   1.11</p>
<p> 2 Portman Min	     390.48   2.46</p>
<p> 3 Niugini Min	     240.29   3.34</p>
<p> 4 Mayne Nickless	  176.82   8.01</p>
<p> 5 TNT			 173.38   2.41</p>
<p> 6 Adel Bton Cement	120.29   1.66</p>
<p> 7 Colonial Coml	   120.22   2.20</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 96.77   2.70</p>
<p> 9 Herald Rsc		 86.73   0.98</p>
<p>10 Westral Forest	   83.33   2.30</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		2.14   0.93</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.91   4.00</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 3.95   0.70</p>
<p> 4 BTR Plc		     5.59   5.20</p>
<p> 5 Queensland Cotton	 5.67   4.30</p>
<p> 6 Parbury Ltd		 6.08   0.72</p>
<p> 7 Aust Gold Rsc	     7.18   1.31</p>
<p> 8 Renison Goldflds	  7.54   5.20</p>
<p> 9 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.56   0.90</p>
<p>10 Templeton Global	  7.88   1.38</p>
